  Thank you for submitting your public records request to the Oregon Park=
s and Recreation Department (OPRD).  =C2=A0  Expect to hear back from us =
in about 10 business days with any records that match your request or, fo=
r larger requests, with an estimate for staff time and costs to gather th=
e documents.  =C2=A0  Thank you,  Oregon Parks and Recreation Department =
=C2=A0     =0D
                           =0D
                            On=0D
                            Sat, 2 May at  6:33 PM=0D
                            ,  Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com>  wro=
te:=0D
                           =0D
                           =0D
                             =0D
 To Whom It May Concern, =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 Pursuant to ORS 192.311 et seq., I am requesting the following records: =
=0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 All public records requests received by the Oregon Parks and Recreation =
Department from January 1, 2023 to present, including for each: the date =
received, the date of agency response, the method of production (electron=
ic or physical mail),=0D
 whether a fee was assessed, whether a fee waiver was requested, whether =
a fee waiver was granted, and whether the request was fulfilled in whole,=
 in part, or denied. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 All written policies, procedures, or guidelines governing the agency's r=
esponse to public records requests, including any internal guidance on pr=
oduction format, fee assessment, and timeline compliance. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 All records reflecting instances where the agency missed the statutory f=
ive-business-day response deadline under ORS 192.324, from January 1, 202=
3 to present. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 All records reflecting the involvement of the OPRD Director, OPRD Interi=
m Director, or OPRD Deputy Director in the review, approval, or direction=
 of responses to public records requests from January 1, 2023 to present,=
 including any communications=0D
 in which executive staff directed the content, timing, or format of a re=
sponse. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 All records reflecting communications between OPRD legal counsel and exe=
cutive staff regarding public records requests, including any guidance on=
 withholding, delaying, or limiting production of records. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 All records reflecting instances where OPRD legal counsel reviewed a pub=
lic records request prior to response, from January 1, 2023 to present. =0D=

 =C2=A0 =0D
 I request that responsive records be produced on a rolling basis as they=
 are identified rather than held until the request is fully processed. =0D=

 =C2=A0 =0D
 Please be advised that I expect all records potentially responsive to th=
is request to be preserved immediately. Any destruction, deletion, modifi=
cation, or alteration of responsive records following receipt of this req=
uest may constitute=0D
 spoliation and will be treated accordingly. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 If any record or portion of a record is withheld, I require the followin=
g for each withheld item: the specific statutory exemption claimed, the d=
ate of the record, the author, and all recipients. A blanket exemption cl=
aim is insufficient=0D
 and will not be accepted as compliance. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 I am requesting a fee waiver on the grounds that this request serves the=
 public interest by enabling public oversight of agency compliance with O=
regon public records law. This request is not commercial in nature. Respo=
nsive records will=0D
 be used to inform and supplement a public archive documenting institutio=
nal conduct, accessible at oprdvolunteerabuse.org. Public access to this =
information advances transparency and accountability in government. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 I am further requesting that all responsive records be produced electron=
ically in PDF or equivalent digital format and delivered to rsw@rswfire.c=
om. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 Please confirm receipt of this request in writing within the statutory f=
ive-business-day window pursuant to ORS 192.324. =0D
 =C2=A0 =0D
 Robert Samuel White =0D
 P.O. Box 334 =0D
 Reedsport, Oregon 97467 =0D
 rsw@rswfire.com =0D
